# Exposure, assumptions, and verification limits

This is one bounded pre-exposure author derivation by the same long-running model family and selected reasoning effort as root. It is not a fresh-context model-independent audit. The worker previously read accepted unary-clock, single-port controller/compiler, and numerous earlier campaign geometry, readiness, and memory sources. Those historical exposures are not erased by the word “independent.” The selected exact sources relevant to this clock problem are pinned in SOURCE_MANIFEST.json; the same mathematical assumptions and prior context were available to root.

For this new task, the root disclosed the neutral target and the existence of a separate construction, but not its conclusion or proof. No directory listing, existence probe, hash, search, or read of the root basis-state-clock candidate occurred. The present freeze must precede any comparison with it. The route was fixed and sent to root before the public prior-art lookup; ROUTE_LOG.md records the subsequent positive-block refinement.

The derivation is self-contained elementary finite-dimensional mathematics: a two-qubit spectral computation, a symmetric-space representation identity, a square-root/binomial variance estimate, and an operator Duhamel estimate. No accepted unary-clock theorem is invoked to assert the new clock bound, and no current controller theorem is silently extended to this clock. The older sources are context and exposure, not undeclared proof dependencies.

The only new external retrieval was the public arXiv abstract for quant-ph/0309131 after the route was fixed. Its exact tool response is WEB_PRIOR_ART_RESPONSE.json. The abstract was read in full; the PDF and paper's full theorem were not read or imported. It supports only the limited prior-art observation explicitly made in the derivation. No novelty claim is made for the engineered weighted spin-chain mechanism. The root candidate remained excluded during this lookup.

Current AGENTS.md, SCIENCE_WORKFLOW.md, and the lane-builder skill were read in this task. Unchanged freshness/writing procedure identities and previously read relevant proof/report sources are recorded by exact identity, with reuse identified as such. The complete new DERIVATION.md was read after drafting and after its two scope/cost additions. No truncated tool response is counted as complete coverage.

There was no scientific executable, numerical fixture, sweep, symbolic package, prior science replay, or new delegation. Metadata programs only copy/hash selected already identified sources, preserve actual launch/stream/exit records, and seal the resulting files. These operations do not verify the mathematics. The analytical checks and failure witnesses are in the derivation itself; a separate review remains necessary before substantial downstream reliance.

The principal supplied contracts are: Hermitian bounded Lipschitz C(t); finite plant H0 and full plant/reference domain; finite sample values or a certified evaluation interface; a known pure single-excitation computational-basis clock, initially independent of the plant/reference input; the positive clock edge terms and static occupation-control interface; adequate calibrated coefficients, energy, timing, and reserves. Literal arbitrary-matrix two-local/geometric implementation, native initialization, indefinite stopping, physical work identification, and reuse are not derived.

The only preliminary route change was replacing scalar-shifted exchange edges by the positive number-weighted blocks in equation (3). No failure is concealed: this was an analytic improvement before the final proof, not an experiment or failed run. The proof preserves the wrong-linear-sampling witness, the vacuum/multi-head domain failure, and the narrow literal two-locality counterexample. None is presented as a universal no-go.

No W, Git ref, PR, audit status, checkpoint, lock, editable prompt, or axiom file was changed. Platform instructions were not modified. All new files are confined to this independent task directory. Publication, acceptance, a comparison with the root candidate, and retained status are pending.
